#!/usr/bin/perl

use strict;
use warnings;
use App::cfvd ();

exit App::cfvd->run( [@ARGV] );

# PODNAME: cfvd
# ABSTRACT: command line interface to CDN::Fast::VCL::Dump

__END__

=head1 SYNOPSIS

 cfvd dump --service <service-id> [--version <n>] <directory>
 cfvd load --service <service-id> --version <n>  <directory>
 cfvd --help

=head1 DESCRIPTION

C<cfvd> dumps a Fastly VCL service version to a directory of plain files and
loads such a directory back into another service version -- possibly on a
different service, version, or customer account.

See L<App::cfvd> for the full list of options and authentication methods, and
L<CDN::Fast::VCL::Dump> for exactly what a dump contains.

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<App::cfvd>, L<CDN::Fast::VCL::Dump>

=cut
